et been processed.  See: Monitor Interchanges\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-21\nValid as Of: 2024-09-21\nVersion: 2408\n\n--- Record 2249 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Cloud Integration: 6.57.*  Increment: 2408  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-21\nValid as Of: 2024-09-21\nVersion: 2408\n\n--- Record 2250 ---\nComponent: Trading Partner Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Update Agreement Properties\nDescription: You can now update the Type System Version for a group of agreements.  See: Update Properties\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-21\nValid as Of: 2024-09-21\nVersion: 2408\n\n", "--- Record 1291 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Correct Condition Base Calculation\nDescription: The pricing condition used to be inactive (inactiveFlag = \"X\") when the from-step number in the pricing procedure was greater than or equal to the step number of the condition during the condition base calculation. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1292 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2025.5\nDescription: New and changed features are available for data integration, data marketplace, data modeling, and others.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2025.5. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-05\nValid as Of: 2025-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1293 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Advanced Functions for Decisions\nDescription: You can now use a new function, DATE in your decisions. See Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-04\nValid as Of: 2025-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1294 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: API Trigger for Decisions\nDescription: You can create an API trigger for a decision to execute this decision using APIs in a shared environment. See Create an API Trigger.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-04\nValid as Of: 2025-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1295 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Export and Import Feature for Documents Used with Instant Learning (Premium Edition)\nDescription: You can now export and import documents that you have edited and confirmed for use with instant learning.  Formerly, instant learning could use your feedback to enhance extraction results only in the client or instance in which you originally edited and confirmed documents. If you changed context, you had to reenter your feedback in the new context.  This new feature on the SAP Document AI basic UI allows you to quickly and easily export documents along with all information relevant for instant learning and import them for use in another context. As a result, you benefit from improved extraction results across different clients and instances, with no additional manual effort.  You can also forward the exported data to your support contact for troubleshooting.  See Export/Import Documents.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-04\nValid as Of: 2025-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1296 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Export Document Details Endpoint\nDescription: The Document API endpoint Export Document Details is now available. Use it to export information that is associated with a document, such as ground truth and related instant learning data.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-04\nValid as Of: 2025-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1297 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models and model versions from Open AI are supported.  For more information, see 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-03\nValid as Of: 2025-03-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1298 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Responses in markdown format from orchestration and prompt editor apps will be rendered in the response window, where supported by the chosen model.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-03\nValid as Of: 2025-03-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1299 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Best Practices for Outlook Activities\nDescription: You can now send emails on behalf of someone in Outlook.See Send Emails on Behalf of Someone in Outlook.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-03\nValid as Of: 2025-03-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1300 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Excel SDK\nDescription: Various Microsoft Excel activities are added to enhance the Microsoft Excel SDK.You can now use the Get Sensitivity Label ID activity to retrieve the sensitivity label ID of the current workbook, the Set Sensitivity activity to set a sensitivity to the current workbook, the Get UsedRange Row (from file) to retrieve the row index of the used range in the active worksheet, the Get UsedRange Column (from file) to retrieve the column index of the used range in the active worksheet and the Get Table Range Definition to retrieve the range definition of a", " to enhance the Microsoft Excel SDK.You can now use the Get Sensitivity Label ID activity to retrieve the sensitivity label ID of the current workbook, the Set Sensitivity activity to set a sensitivity to the current workbook, the Get UsedRange Row (from file) to retrieve the row index of the used range in the active worksheet, the Get UsedRange Column (from file) to retrieve the column index of the used range in the active worksheet and the Get Table Range Definition to retrieve the range definition of a named table in the active worksheet.See Excel SDK and Best Practices for Excel Activities - Get Sensitivity Label ID.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-03\nValid as Of: 2025-03-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2901 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: New Property ABAP Language Version\nDescription: You can now use the new property abaplv to filter your object searches with the ABAP language version.  See Property Filter.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2902 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Scheduling of Custom Code Migration Projects via Application Jobs\nDescription: Through the Schedule Custom Code Analysis app, you can now schedule projects created in the Custom Code Migration app as application jobs. With this functionality, their analyses can be performed periodically. The Schedule Custom Code Analysis app is available to all users that have access to the Custom Code Migration app.For more information, see Custom Code Analysis.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-08\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2903 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Software Component Relations Editor\nDescription: You can now use the software component relations editor to create software component relations that define access permissions and dependencies between productive custom development software components.  See Working with Software Component Relations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2904 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Template Contexts When Creating Metadata Extensions\nDescription: The former template context for metadata extensions has been replaced with the two new contexts Annotate Entity (creation) and Annotate View (creation).  See Creating Metadata Extensions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2905 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Test Code Highlighting for Method Calls\nDescription: You can now use test code highlighting to get a quick visual overview of method calls that are used in unit test classes. Different colors are used to distinguish between various method contexts.  See Test Code Highlighting.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2906 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Toggling The Step Size in The ABAP Debugger\nDescription: While running the ABAP Debugger, you can now switch between the following two step modes:      Step Size: 'Line' to step from one line to the next.  Note  This is the default mode.      Step Size: 'Expression' changes the behavior for:      more than one statement in a single line.      conditional expressions and expressions.          See Toggling the Step Size.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2907 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Tool Bridges Between ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse and VSCode/BAS\nDescription: It's now possible to provide tool bridges that streamline the UI development flow between backend ABAP service development in ADT and frontend SAPUI5/Fiori Elements development in BAS/VSCode.  See Creating a Fiori Project.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-16\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2908 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Using Quick Actions to Insert ABAP Unit Test Class Templates\nDescription: You can now use quick actions to insert templates for ABAP Unit test classes with just a single mouse click.  See How to Write ABAP Unit Test Classes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2909 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Entity Assignment of RAP Business Events\nDescription: You can now assign RAP business events to entities that are not defined as root entity.  For more information on business events, see RAP Business Events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2910", ": Entity Assignment of RAP Business Events\nDescription: You can now assign RAP business events to entities that are not defined as root entity.  For more information on business events, see RAP Business Events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2910 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Factory Calendar Pull Integration\nDescription: You can now integrate the S/4HANA Cloud data from your factory calendar into the SAP BTP, ABAP environment to keep them in sync. A pull integration is available that pulls the data from the SAP S/4HANA system and inserts it in the SAP BTP, ABAP environment. Doing this, you can avoid double maintenance, and factory calendar calculations can still be done locally for optimal performance.  For more information, see Integrating Factory Calendar.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n", "--- Record 2491 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for Build-Code Service Plan\nDescription: If you're using Document Management Service, Integration Optionand Document Management Service, Application Option as part of SAP Build Code, a separate build-code subscription plan is available.  To subscribe or to update to the build-code subscription plan from your current subscriptions, use the SAP Build Code booster.  See:  Service Plans  Updating the Service Plan  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2492 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Terminology Change in the SAP Document Mobile Application\nDescription: The option under the user menu Check for Updates has been renamed to Check for App Updates. Only the name has been changed and there is no change in the functionality.  See User Menu.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2493 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Usage Data Management section and event\nDescription: You can now use the newly supported Usage Data Management Remaining Credits event. For more information, see Usage Data Management section page.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2494 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Maximum Instance Memory Increased to 16 GB\nDescription: We have increased the maximum limit for runtime memory per application instance from 8 GB to 16 GB. This also means that the guaranteed CPU capacity per application instance can now be scaled up to 4 CPU cores.  For more information, see SAP BTP-Specific Configurations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2495 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 41.1.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 40.18.0 to 41.1.0.    https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v41.1.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v41.0.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v40.19.0  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2496 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Bug Fix\nDescription: The following issue has been resolved: Web content card can’t be displayed in a full screen mode.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: 2407B\n\n--- Record 2497 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change of Image Size Limitation\nDescription: Until now, any image file larger than 5MB (1024*1024*5 pixels) was rejected when uploaded to the image widget and it wouldn't be recognized as an image when uploaded to workspace content.  With the new behavior, for images uploaded to the Content folder, a preview is available for images up to 20MB. Above 20MB, a preview will not be available. For images uploaded directly to the image widget, 20M is the new size limit.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: 2407B\n\n--- Record 2498 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Content Thumbnail Image Crop\nDescription: Thumbnail images used for wikis, blogs, or KBAs can be adjusted using a slider or dragging the image so that it’s displayed properly in content widgets with different layouts (thumbnail/gallery/carousel) and in the Content list in grid view.  This also applies to the thumbnail image that’s added to a video widget.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: 2407B\n\n--- Record 2499 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Notification Enhancements\nDescription: The workspace notification UI has been enhanced when using the central notification of BTP. The following issues have been fixed: notification labels, invitation-related actions, and notification types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid", "2407B\n\n--- Record 2499 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Notification Enhancements\nDescription: The workspace notification UI has been enhanced when using the central notification of BTP. The following issues have been fixed: notification labels, invitation-related actions, and notification types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: 2407B\n\n--- Record 2500 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Mapping Cards to Destinations\nDescription: Administrators can now map cards to destinations.  After creating a new content channel that contains cards, the administrator must map any destinations defined in the cards to runtime destinations defined in the SAP BTP cockpit.   To do this, use the Map Aliases option, located in the Status column of the channel in the Channel Manager, and map the destinations in the Cards Aliases tab (new).  Note that the mapping is required for new content channels. Existing channels will continue to work with no further actions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-08\nValid as Of: 2024-08-08\nVersion: 2407B\n\n", "--- Record 3071 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation/Decommissioning of Machine Learning Operators and Image Tags\nDescription: The SAP Data Intelligence Machine Learning Guide now includes a section that provides updates about the Machine Learning components. In this section, you can find information about deprecated operators, image tags, and applications. The section includes the timeline for the complete removal of the components with appropriate replacements.  For more information, see Deprecation of Machine Learning Components and SAP Note 2958072 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3072 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: End of SAP Data Intelligence Cloud Maintenance\nDescription: To enable secure planning and to support a sufficient transition phase from SAP Data Intelligence Cloud to SAP Datasphere, SAP provides maintenance for SAP Data Intelligence Cloud until December 31, 2028.  For more information, see 3423165  and https://community.sap.com/t5/technology-blogs-by-sap/sap-datasphere-and-sap-data-intelligence-cloud-what-does-this-mean-for-me/ba-p/13603947 on the SAP Community website.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3073 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Google BigQuery Table Loader Operator Deprecated\nDescription: The Google BigQuery Table Loader operator (com.sap.dh.ds.gbq.producer) is deprecated. Upgrade to Generation 2 Cloud Table Producer (com.sap.cloud.table.producer) operator.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3074 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Kafka Operators Support for Embedded Credentials\nDescription: Kafka operators now support new fields available in the Kafka connection for embedded credentials.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3075 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Microsoft SQL Server 2022 Support\nDescription: You can now create MSSQL connections with the version \"Microsoft SQL Server 2022\" to connect to databases with this version.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3076 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pipeline Engine Runtime API Support for Tenant-Wide Requests\nDescription: Monitoring and administrative users can now get tenant-wide graph runtime data.  For more information, see SAP Business Accelerator Hub.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3077 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Python Updated to 3.9\nDescription: The Python environment in the Machine Learning tools for SAP Data Intelligence has been updated to Python 3.9. This change provides a more updated and standardized environment. The JupyterLab version has also been increased.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3078 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Reduce Duplicate Records During Initial Load\nDescription: Duplicate part files in the target object store have been frequently observed after the RMS worker graph crashed. This update tries to minimize the creation of duplicate part files when performing replications of initial load type into object store target.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3079 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Cloud Connector and SFTP Connections\nDescription: The SFTP (SSH File Transfer Protocol) connection type now supports connecting to on-premise sources with the SAP Cloud Connector.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3080 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Send Email operator (Generation 2) Available\nDescription: The Send Email operator is now available in Generation 2.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 31 ---\nComponent: Joule,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Navigational Use Cases Added to Joule in SAP BTP Cockpit\nDescription: Within a Cloud Foundry space, Joule in the cockpit can now take you to the following pages:  Service Marketplace  Routes  Security Groups    For more information, check out Supported Administrative Tasks Using Joule in the Cockpit\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-22\nValid as Of: 2025-07-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 32 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Enhancements\nDescription:   Co-referencing of Complex Message TypesComplex message types can now be co-referenced in chats. This allows users to reference previous non-text outputs, ensuring coherent and context-aware conversations.  Propagate Error Message for User-Transparent and Understandable LLM Error HandlingTransparent error handling in Joule ensures that users receive clear and understandable messages about specific errors, such as content filter violations and length restrictions. This allows users to continue their conversations seamlessly, enhancing the overall user experience by minimising confusion and interruptions.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-15\nValid as Of: 2025-07-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 33 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Support for Documents in JSON and PPTX File Formats\nDescription: The document grounding capability now supports documents in JSON and PPTX file formats for the following providers and regions:  Amazon Web Services eu10 - Europe (Frankfurt), eu11 - Europe (Frankfurt) EU Access, and us10 - US East (VA)  Google Cloud eu30 - Europe (Frankfurt) and us30 - US Central (IA)  Microsoft Azure eu20 - Europe (Netherlands) and us21 - US East (VA)    See Set Up Document Grounding.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-11\nValid as Of: 2025-07-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 34 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Support for Integration with SAP Build Work Zone\nDescription: The document grounding capability now supports the integration with SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition.  See Set Up Data Repository Integration, Configure Access from SAP BTP, and Set Up Content Ingestion.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-11\nValid as Of: 2025-07-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 35 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Navigation Now Available in SAP Integrated Business Planning\nDescription: You can now use Joule to find and navigate to apps in SAP Integrated Business Planning.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-04\nValid as Of: 2025-07-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 36 ---\nComponent: Joule,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Administrative Use Cases Added to Joule in the SAP BTP Cockpit\nDescription: We've added to the list of administrative tasks that Joule can assist you with in the SAP BTP Cockpit:     Joule can now add new users to an existing subaccount  Select informational use cases now include a navigation option to have Joule take you to the corresponding cockpit page   Navigate to trust configuration in either the global account or a subaccount   Navigate to service instances in a Cloud Foundry space    For more information, check out Supported Administrative Tasks with Joule in the Cockpit\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-02\nValid as Of: 2025-07-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 37 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Project assistant capabilities for Joule – Read Project sub-elements and Summarize changes to Projects & WBS Elements\nDescription: The following transactional use cases are now supported in Enterprise Portfolio and Project Management for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition:     Display WBS elements and Networks assigned to a project or WBS element  Summarize the changes of Projects and WBS Elements  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-24\nValid as Of: 2025-06-26\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 38 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Analytical Insights Capability - Support for Integration with SAP Build Work Zone\nDescription: The analytical insights capability in Joule now requires SAP Analytics Cloud integration with SAP Build Work Zone to allow users access to the feature. Users, roles, and permissions from SAP Analytics Cloud can be synced with SAP Build Work Zone by administrators using the provided instructions. This allows for role-based access and gives you greater flexibility in determining who in your organization can use analytical insights.  For more information, see Integration with SAP Analytics Cloud.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-24\nValid", " Work Zone to allow users access to the feature. Users, roles, and permissions from SAP Analytics Cloud can be synced with SAP Build Work Zone by administrators using the provided instructions. This allows for role-based access and gives you greater flexibility in determining who in your organization can use analytical insights.  For more information, see Integration with SAP Analytics Cloud.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-24\nValid as Of: 2025-06-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 39 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases for SAP SuccessFactors Available in Joule - June 2025\nDescription: The following Joule use cases are now available in SAP SuccessFactors:      Fix login issues      View company      For more information, refer to New Use Cases Available in Joule - June 2025.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-24\nValid as Of: 2025-06-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 40 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Now Supported in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: Joule 